{0 Immutable tmux values and typed queries}

{!Libtmux} is the pure core. Capture through an optional client backend, then
inspect and filter immutable observations with ordinary OCaml collections.

{1 Read the graph}

Start with {!Libtmux.Snapshot}, {!Libtmux.Session}, {!Libtmux.Window_link},
{!Libtmux.Window} and {!Libtmux.Pane}. A window link owns session-specific index
and current state. Captured relationships never perform I/O.

{1 Select before acting}

Use [Seq.filter] for application predicates or {!Libtmux.Expr} for typed,
inspectable expressions. {!Libtmux.Query.exactly_one} distinguishes absence
from ambiguity before submitting a mutation.

{[
# open Libtmux;;
# let roomy = Expr.Int.ge Pane.Fields.width 80;;
val roomy : Pane.t Expr.t = <abstr>
# Query.exactly_one (List.to_seq [42]);;
- : (int, Cardinality.error) result = Ok 42
# Query.exactly_one (List.to_seq [42; 42]);;
- : (int, Cardinality.error) result =
Error (Cardinality.Multiple_matches {Libtmux.Cardinality.at_least = 2})
]}

{!Libtmux.Operations} constructs commands. It does not execute them. Optional
blocking and Eio packages own connections, cancellation and output subscriptions.

{1 Inspect a source-filter plan}

{!Libtmux.Plan.panes} plans without I/O. Backend capture operations still acquire
the complete graph; an acquisition adapter must consume a plan explicitly.

{[
# let planned =
    match Plan.panes ~pushdown:Require_exact
            (Expr.Bool.is_true Pane.Fields.active) with
    | Ok plan -> plan
    | Error error -> failwith (Format.asprintf "%a" Error.pp error);;
val planned : Plan.t = <abstr>
# Option.is_some (Plan.source_filter planned);;
- : bool = true
]}

{1 Identity and failure}

{!Libtmux.Source} binds IDs to one connection generation. Entity identity differs
from observation identity; old targets cannot silently retarget a new daemon.
Expected errors use {!Libtmux.Error}. Snapshots represent an acquisition interval,
not an atomic server transaction.
